{"name":"Ilmwatch","status":"ok","title":"Ilmwatch","pageId":71088,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\" role=\"region\">\n\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Maps_of_Ilmwatch\" title=\"Category:Maps of Ilmwatch\">Gallery</a></nav>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Ilmwatch</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Geography<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-TBL-p28_1-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TBL-p28-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p191_2-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p191-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"type\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Fortress-town</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"region\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Buzzard_Beak_Harbor\" title=\"Buzzard Beak Harbor\">Buzzard Beak Harbor</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Impiltur\" title=\"Impiltur\">Impiltur</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">History<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-TBL-p28_1-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TBL-p28-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p191_2-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p191-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"population1\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Population</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">560 in <a href=\"/wiki/1359_DR\" title=\"1359 DR\">1359 DR</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"ruler1\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Ruler</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSGVza2FyX0JyYW5kb3NrP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\" title=\"Heskar Brandosk (page does not exist)\">Heskar Brandosk</span> in <a href=\"/wiki/1372_DR\" title=\"1372 DR\">1372 DR</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</aside>\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b>Ilmwatch</b> was a large fortress-town that protected the infamous <a href=\"/wiki/Buzzard_Beak_Harbor\" title=\"Buzzard Beak Harbor\">Buzzard Beak Harbor</a> and traders of the <a href=\"/wiki/Merchant%27s_Run\" title=\"Merchant's Run\">Merchant's Run</a>, located on the northern end of the <a href=\"/wiki/Easting_Reach\" title=\"Easting Reach\">Easting Reach</a>, within the <a href=\"/wiki/Farwater\" title=\"Farwater\">Farwater</a> region of <a href=\"/wiki/Impiltur\" title=\"Impiltur\">Impiltur</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-TBL-p28_1-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TBL-p28-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-TBL.M_3-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TBL.M-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p191_2-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p191-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\" class=\"toc\" id=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\"><input class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" role=\"button\" style=\"display:none\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"toctitle\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Description\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Description</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Activities\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Activities</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#History\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">History</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Appendix\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appendix</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Description\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ilmwatch?veaction=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Description\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Despite its strategic location between Impiltur and <a href=\"/wiki/Damara\" title=\"Damara\">Damara</a>, Ilmwatch was not a particularly busy port city.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p191_2-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p191-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Activities\">Activities</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Activities\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ilmwatch?veaction=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Activities\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>During most months of the year, sea-travel from the <a href=\"/wiki/Sea_of_Fallen_Stars\" title=\"Sea of Fallen Stars\">Sea of Fallen Stars</a> was largely navigable along the <a href=\"/wiki/Great_Imphras_River\" title=\"Great Imphras River\">Great Imphras River</a> until the great city of <a href=\"/wiki/Helgabal\" title=\"Helgabal\">Helgabal</a>. As such, Ilmwatch only brought in a few ships that unloaded their goods within the fortress. The settlement did see some overland trade, primarily from smaller mercantile operations that only required wagons or horses as a means of conveyance.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p191_2-4\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p191-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Ilmwatch was large enough to easily support several hundred troops. Soldiers from the <a href=\"/wiki/Warswords\" title=\"Warswords\">Warswords</a> were tasked with protecting merchants traveling to and from Damara as well as those who crossed the Easting Reach to <a href=\"/wiki/Uthmere\" title=\"Uthmere\">Uthmere</a>. Patrols regularly scouted the surrounding lands and often accompanied merchants traveling along the Merchant's Run and <a href=\"/wiki/Herald%27s_Road\" title=\"Herald's Road\">Herald's Road</a>, as they passed closer to the fortress. Their influence extended as far north as Uthmerg to the southwestern local known as the <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvTmFycm93cz9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Narrows (page does not exist)\">Narrows</span>, where the Herald's Road crossed the <a href=\"/wiki/Bluefang_Water\" title=\"Bluefang Water\">Bluefang Water</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-TBL-p28_1-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TBL-p28-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p191_2-5\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p191-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DM:346.I_4-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DM:346.I-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: History\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ilmwatch?veaction=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: History\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Ilmwatch was founded by <a href=\"/wiki/Ilmara\" title=\"Ilmara\">Ilmara</a>, sister of <a href=\"/wiki/Imbrar_I\" title=\"Imbrar I\">Imbrar I</a>, during his brief rule. There, she used the Scrying Stones of <a href=\"/wiki/Myth_Drannor\" title=\"Myth Drannor\">Myth Drannor</a> to guard against the return of the hogboblin forces defeated by her father <a href=\"/wiki/Imphras_I\" title=\"Imphras I\">Imphras I</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-CoV-pp88_5-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-CoV-pp88-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>During the late 14<sup>th</sup> century <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/DR\" title=\"DR\">DR</a>, Ilmwatch was governed by <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSGVza2FyX0JyYW5kb3NrP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\" title=\"Heskar Brandosk (page does not exist)\">Heskar Brandosk</span>. He led a stalwart defense of the fortress against the influence of the <a href=\"/wiki/Shadowmasters_of_Telflamm\" title=\"Shadowmasters of Telflamm\">Shadowmasters</a> of <a href=\"/wiki/Telflamm\" title=\"Telflamm\">Telflamm</a> and pirates that scoured the coast of the Easting Reach.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p191_2-6\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p191-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appendix\">Appendix</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Appendix\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ilmwatch?veaction=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Appendix\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: References\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ilmwatch?veaction=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: References\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div class=\"reflist\" style=\"\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-TBL-p28-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TBL-p28_1-0\">1.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TBL-p28_1-1\">1.1</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TBL-p28_1-2\">1.2</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TBL-p28_1-3\">1.3</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/R.A._Salvatore\" title=\"R.A. Salvatore\">R.A. Salvatore</a> (1989). <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Bloodstone_Lands_(sourcebook)\" title=\"The Bloodstone Lands (sourcebook)\">The Bloodstone Lands</a></i>. Edited by <a href=\"/wiki/Elizabeth_T._Danforth\" title=\"Elizabeth T. Danforth\">Elizabeth T. Danforth</a>. (<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/TSR,_Inc\" title=\"TSR, Inc\">TSR, Inc</a>), p. 28. ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/0-88038-771-8\" title=\"Special:BookSources/0-88038-771-8\">0-88038-771-8</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-UE-p191-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-UE-p191_2-0\">2.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-UE-p191_2-1\">2.1</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-UE-p191_2-2\">2.2</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-UE-p191_2-3\">2.3</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-UE-p191_2-4\">2.4</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-UE-p191_2-5\">2.5</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-UE-p191_2-6\">2.6</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Richard_Baker\" title=\"Richard Baker\">Richard Baker</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Matt_Forbeck\" title=\"Matt Forbeck\">Matt Forbeck</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Sean_K._Reynolds\" title=\"Sean K. Reynolds\">Sean K. Reynolds</a> (May 2003). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Unapproachable_East_(sourcebook)\" title=\"Unapproachable East (sourcebook)\">Unapproachable East</a></i>. (<a href=\"/wiki/Wizards_of_the_Coast\" title=\"Wizards of the Coast\">Wizards of the Coast</a>). ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/0-7869-2881-6\" title=\"Special:BookSources/0-7869-2881-6\">0-7869-2881-6</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-TBL.M-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-TBL.M_3-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/R.A._Salvatore\" title=\"R.A. Salvatore\">R.A. Salvatore</a> (1989). <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Bloodstone_Lands_(sourcebook)\" title=\"The Bloodstone Lands (sourcebook)\">The Bloodstone Lands (Map)</a></i>. (<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/TSR,_Inc\" title=\"TSR, Inc\">TSR, Inc</a>). ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/0-88038-771-8\" title=\"Special:BookSources/0-88038-771-8\">0-88038-771-8</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-DM:346.I-4\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-DM:346.I_4-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/George_Krashos\" title=\"George Krashos\">George Krashos</a> (August 2006). “Impiltur: The Forgotten Kingdom”. In <a href=\"/wiki/Erik_Mona\" title=\"Erik Mona\">Erik Mona</a> ed. <a href=\"/wiki/Dragon_magazine_346\" title=\"Dragon magazine 346\"><i>Dragon</i> #346</a> (<a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.paizo.com\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Paizo Publishing, LLC</a>), pp. 56–71.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-CoV-pp88-5\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-CoV-pp88_5-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Thomas_M._Reid\" title=\"Thomas M. Reid\">Thomas M. Reid</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Sean_K._Reynolds\" title=\"Sean K. Reynolds\">Sean K. Reynolds</a> (Nov. 2005). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Champions_of_Valor\" title=\"Champions of Valor\">Champions of Valor</a></i>. (<a href=\"/wiki/Wizards_of_the_Coast\" title=\"Wizards of the Coast\">Wizards of the Coast</a>), p. 88. ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/0-7869-3697-5\" title=\"Special:BookSources/0-7869-3697-5\">0-7869-3697-5</a>.</span>\n</li>\n</ol></div>\n</div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260517065030\nCache expiry: 1209600\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.077 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.143 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1479/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 6527/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 3288/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 14/100\nExpensive parser function count: 1/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5089/5000000 bytes\nExtLoops count: 0/200\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%  103.921      1 -total\n 45.62% 